From 0fb36a5e2e3692b95f7127ef87b102b1d62d2a90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joop Kiefte <ikojba@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:15:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Add The Puzzle Pits engine (game_pits)

The Puzzle Pits (Abe Pralle, Plasma Works, 1995) is a Sokoban-like
puzzle game with scripted levels. This engine plays its own level files
(LEVELnn.PIT) by its own rules, drawn from its own pictures (TILES1.DAT
to TILES3.DAT), with its sounds (*.WAV):

- the rules: pushing, the tile rules (water, lava, holes, wood, glass,
  arrows, coloured targets), plates, switches, signs, gems and keys,
  winning when every target holds its colour
- the scripts: the game's own language, run as the game runs them;
  their text in R'n'D's envelopes, a page at a time; a script that asks
  for typed text (INPUT) opens a room of letter keys, and one that asks
  for a square (TARGET) a cursor
- the pit drawn as the game draws it, objects reaching over the squares
  beside them, around the player, filling the playfield
- turns counted from frames only, so tapes replay

Keys: directions; snap with a direction uses a gem (left red, up green,
right blue, down yellow), drop with a direction a key (left red, up
green, right blue); snap alone waits a turn. Mouse: the left button
steps towards a square, the right one walks there.

Written from a description of the game (PITS-RULES.md and PIT-FORMAT.md,
https://github.com/LaPingvino/The-Puzzle-Pits/tree/master/docs), not
from its code.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
